<title>INDIA: Indian gold, silver trade shut in tax protest.</title>
<headline>Indian gold, silver trade shut in tax protest.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1997-01-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Indian gold and silver markets were closed on Thursday in a protest by traders over increased tax costs, dealers said.</p>
<p>On Wednesday, silver prices gained on reports of world market gains while gold weakened on poor overseas trends.</p>
<p>Traders are protesting an increase in sales tax and other charges from January 1 by the government in the western Maharashtra state, where Bombay is located.</p>
<p>Trading will resume on Friday.</p>
<p>-- Bombay commodities +91-22-265 9000</p>
</text>
